x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 form of a constructor defined inside its class on this target, and a constructor template's specialization can be defined nowhere else; cxx1 emits C1 beside it (_ZN3BoxI1MEC1IRS0_EEOT_ and the two others). arm64-darwin, which emits both, agrees on all 13 names, the forwarded U = M & spelled RS0_ as clang spells it; x86_64-windows agrees on all 7.
